fore his time,¦layout ‚¤textÙ"And his branch shall not be green.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And shall cast off his flower as the olive.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ5For the congregation of hypocrites shall be desolate,¦layout ‚¤textÙ2And fire shall consume the tabernacles of bribery.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/They conceive mischief, and bring forth vanity,¦layout ‚¤textÙ!And their belly prepareth deceit.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#